A||N||24||Haze_Performance||Need all 4 cylinder performance info.........||||1||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||09-27-2001||05:41 PM||||I'm looking for anyone that has modified there 4 cylinder (2.5L Duke & Trans. Auto,4 or 5 Speed) <P>I need information (Brand, Part #'s, How much did it cost, Where did you buy it, Ease of Install) on any & all modifications done. Right now I just need: <P>Any Engine Mods... (Cam, Ignition TB, Headwork, Intake...ect) <P>Any Trans Mods... (Coolers, Torque Converter, Clutch...ect) <P>I have a Club meeting coming up. I along with Oreif, are going to talk about Fiero Performance. I have the task of 4 cylinder Performance. I appreciate any and all input. I'm going to print out a page or two of info to pass out at the meeting. If you have a detailed mod, I can add your email address to the page. (People can email you & ask about you mod in greater detail) <P>Thank You <BR>-Haze  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">      .      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">      .      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/9112001.gif"> <BR><I><B><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners</B></I></FONT> - <FONT COLOR="red"><A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000001||baldlobo||09-27-2001||06:43 PM||||lets see <BR>Cams: <A HREF="http://camcraftcams.com/index2.html" TARGET=_blank>http://camcraftcams.com/index2.html</A>  <A HREF="http://www.compcams.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.compcams.com/</A>  <A HREF="http://www.iskycams.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.iskycams.com/</A>  <A HREF="http://www.ultradyne.com/pontiac_151_4_cylinder.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ultradyne.com/pontiac_151_4_cylinder.htm</A>  <A HREF="http://www.cranecams.com/master/apps/pontiac1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cranecams.com/master/apps/pontiac1.htm</A> <P>Other engine parts <A HREF="http://www.cliffordperformance.com/main.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cliffordperformance.com/main.htm</A> <BR>https://www.spoperformanceparts.com/ <A HREF="http://www.holley.com/nIndex.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.holley.com/nIndex.html</A>  <A HREF="http://www.msdignition.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.msdignition.com/</A> <P><BR>don't bother asking me if I've used any of these parts(my car is still in the repair phase(and I'm still in the need of a job phase))  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||09-27-2001||07:27 PM||||<BR>Hey Haze!<BR>Here is a kinda step by step...<P>Pull the Duke, and put on engine stand...<P>Disassemble to bare block, discard all internal and external parts...<P>Attach rope to new boat anchor (block), and remove from engine stand...<P>Install new/used super duty block to engine stand...<P>Install new internal and external parts...<P>Remove from engine stand and install in car...<P><BR>Now, if you don't want to invest $20,000 in an engine, find a buick or olds with a 3800 V6 for $100 to $500, pull it and rebuild stock, or mildly warmed over, and have a screaming Fiero!<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||09-27-2001||07:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by baldlobo:<BR><B>lets see <BR>Cams: <A HREF="http://camcraftcams.com/index2.html" TARGET=_blank>http://camcraftcams.com/index2.html</A>  <A HREF="http://www.compcams.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.compcams.com/</A>  <A HREF="http://www.iskycams.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.iskycams.com/</A>  <A HREF="http://www.ultradyne.com/pontiac_151_4_cylinder.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ultradyne.com/pontiac_151_4_cylinder.htm</A>  <A HREF="http://www.cranecams.com/master/apps/pontiac1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cranecams.com/master/apps/pontiac1.htm</A> <P>Other engine parts <A HREF="http://www.cliffordperformance.com/main.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cliffordperformance.com/main.htm</A> <BR>https://www.spoperformanceparts.com/ <A HREF="http://www.holley.com/nIndex.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.holley.com/nIndex.html</A>  <A HREF="http://www.msdignition.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.msdignition.com/</A> <P><BR>don't bother asking me if I've used any of these parts(my car is still in the repair phase(and I'm still in the need of a job phase))   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks baldlobo...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierowrecker:<BR><B><BR>Hey Haze!<BR>Here is a kinda step by step...<P>Pull the Duke, and put on engine stand...<P>Disassemble to bare block, discard all internal and external parts...<P>Attach rope to new boat anchor (block), and remove from engine stand...<P>Install new/used super duty block to engine stand...<P>Install new internal and external parts...<P>Remove from engine stand and install in car...<P><BR>Now, if you don't want to invest $20,000 in an engine, find a buick or olds with a 3800 V6 for $100 to $500, pull it and rebuild stock, or mildly warmed over, and have a screaming Fiero!<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Fierowrecker,<BR> I need 4 banger part & part # info for the meeting. I cant tell the 4 cylinder purists to pull out there engines.. lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">      .      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">      .      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/9112001.gif"> <BR><I><B><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners</B></I></FONT> - <FONT COLOR="red"><A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||09-27-2001||08:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B> Hey Fierowrecker,<BR> I need 4 banger part & part # info for the meeting. I cant tell the 4 cylinder purists to pull out there engines.. lol   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Haze!<BR>Glad you are laughing, as it was meant as a joke!<BR>Course, you could print it out anyways!!!<BR>I know, I am soooo mean some times!!!<BR>crash...<BR>(Let the flames begin!)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Galen||09-27-2001||08:42 PM||||Perhaps it is meant as a joke, but I find that it embodies the thoughts of alot of people, that at the very thought of someone 'attempting' to tweak a duke, that its their god given right as a a$$hole to bash on em. You do not embrace the idea that some people do not wish to swap engines. Now am I calling you a a$$hole? Perhaps, but its my god given right as a duke owner to do that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/g-flag-sig.gif">  <FONT COLOR="purple">1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe</FONT> - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Leper||09-27-2001||09:59 PM||||Performace parts eh?<BR>Part numbers?<P>Super Duty block 10093306 $836.65 <BR>Super duty engine hardware package 10031328 $129.44 <BR>Super duty head 10045437 $937.32 <BR>or the high port version 10049801 $1,230.14 <BR>Intake manifold gasket 12371032 $18.16 <BR>Super duty cam gears 10037684 $196.43 <BR>4bbl super duty intake manifold 10038470 233.54<BR>Super duty distrubuter 10037373 $341.90 <BR>total $3232.15<BR>Only thing left is the rotating assembly and the cam. I think Lunati still sels the parts.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||09-28-2001||12:29 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/fiero2m4/IronDuke.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/fiero2m4/IronDuke.html</A> <P>I did an article for my newsletter about Duke performance and used this site heavily.  Probably the best source on the web for Dukes that I have seen.<P>If you want I can send you the article as well. Its pretty generalized but the pictures are worth it.<P>Just e-mail me.||||reg||2
Z||000008||KissMySSFiero||09-28-2001||01:54 PM||||Haze,<BR>when is the meeting?  is it in october?<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000009||qwikgta||09-28-2001||08:59 PM||||Some perf, some looks<P>Header, ebay, $200<BR>Valve cover w/ threaded twist off cap, jyard $20<BR>Ultimate bone, Fiero Store, $50<BR>Homemade air cleaner W/ K&N Filter, $30/$20<BR>2 1/4 exhaust pipe, local shop, $40<BR>Supertrapp, Ebay, $28<BR>Remove A/C and replace belt w/ nonA/C belt, $10<P>Pics<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/air_cleaner0002.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/header_shot2.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/air_cleaner0004.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/my_engine4.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1july11_1.jpg"> <P>Rob<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fierowrecker||09-28-2001||10:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>Perhaps it is meant as a joke, but I find that it embodies the thoughts of alot of people, that at the very thought of someone 'attempting' to tweak a duke, that its their god given right as a a$$hole to bash on em. You do not embrace the idea that some people do not wish to swap engines. Now am I calling you a a$$hole? Perhaps, but its my god given right as a duke owner to do that.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Guess I am a double a$$hole times four then?<BR>As I own four iron pukes...<BR>And if I am bashing any one, I am bashing myself as well...<BR>So if I ever complete the 3800 swap I am doing, then I double the a$$hole quotient, making me the biggest A$$HOLE on the board!!!<BR>At least I am number one at something, I may as well be the biggest a$$hole!!!<P>And I reiterate, I have hopped up one iron puke, and it lived up to it's name and PUKED!!!<BR>I am just giving the benefit of my experience as a puke owner, that the puke is a useless hunk of pig iron to hop up and expect to survive very long...<BR>So if others do not want to heed my advise but follow in my foot steps and build up a puke, spending their hard earned money, just to flush it down the toilet, be my guest!!!<BR>But when I blow their doors off and their engine starts billowing big blue clouds of smoke, they will wish they had listened...<BR>DEATH TO THE PUKE!!! LONG LIVE THE SIX!!!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fierowrecker||09-28-2001||10:47 PM||||Hey Rob!<BR>Excellent looking engine and compartment!<BR>What year is that Fiero?<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000012||TI_3VOM||09-29-2001||02:37 PM||||...as copied from the main page at  <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/fiero2m4/IronDuke.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/fiero2m4/IronDuke.html</A> <P><BR>This page is not meant to send you out looking for a four cylinder Fiero to build a performance car.   The 2.8L V6 Fiero offers far more "Bang for the Buck" since they cost only a little more and have 50% more horsepower.   This is aimed more at the owner who wants to try something different, BUT EXPENSIVE, like building an SD4,  or someone who already has a 2.5 and would just like to try some of the more modest suggestions to make their cars more enjoyable.<P>...sounds like a lot of us 2.5 owners, especially the last half of the last sentence.||||reg||1
Z||000013||fotofrank||09-29-2001||09:23 PM||||Haxe, <BR>Hooker Header(tri-y) e-bay about $210.00<BR>Holley intake (no longer in production) e-bay $ 200.00<BR>Holley TB private sale $95.00<BR>MSD6A e-bay $100.00<BR>MSD GM blaster coil MSD $45.00<BR>K&N filter e-bay $20.00<BR>Valve job $95.00<P>Can't say I've got hundreds of HP but it's mine and I and my son did all the work (excepting valve job). it now has fine throtle responce and some amout of a$$ o meter improvement on lounch. The car now gets noticeable faster to 60 mph and faster. Have not taken it past 95mph as of yet. A little morework on the valve lash and timing and away she goes. I would like to install a preformance cam, maybe an ISKY. I figure that with the bolt ons and cam the engine will not be stressed much and yet give acceptable preformance.<BR>Working with a Duke is a chalange and I'm sure all you V-8 and V-6 types can understand that. It is not always the satisfaction of being the fastes but getting what one can from what one has that counts. What do you say to that? Flame, flame, flame if you want. <P><P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||6
Z||000014||Fierowrecker||09-30-2001||01:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fotofrank:<BR><B>Haxe, <BR>Hooker Header(tri-y) e-bay about $210.00<BR>Holley intake (no longer in production) e-bay $ 200.00<BR>Holley TB private sale $95.00<BR>MSD6A e-bay $100.00<BR>MSD GM blaster coil MSD $45.00<BR>K&N filter e-bay $20.00<BR>Valve job $95.00<P>Can't say I've got hundreds of HP but it's mine and I and my son did all the work (excepting valve job). it now has fine throtle responce and some amout of a$$ o meter improvement on lounch. The car now gets noticeable faster to 60 mph and faster. Have not taken it past 95mph as of yet. A little morework on the valve lash and timing and away she goes. I would like to install a preformance cam, maybe an ISKY. I figure that with the bolt ons and cam the engine will not be stressed much and yet give acceptable preformance.<BR>Working with a Duke is a chalange and I'm sure all you V-8 and V-6 types can understand that. It is not always the satisfaction of being the fastes but getting what one can from what one has that counts. What do you say to that? Flame, flame, flame if you want. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thank You Frank!<BR>An honest, and respectable opinion as to what you are trying to accomplish!<BR>I wish you luck in your endevor to improve your car, and may you enjoy it as long as I have had my four 2M4's...<BR>I do have a question though, did you have standard or roller lifters?<BR>I had 2 86 engines with rollers, and several of them were broke when I disassembled them...<BR>I ended up rebuilding an 84 so I had standard lifters...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000015||SLYGUY||09-30-2001||02:55 AM||||A 2.8 V6 is a good step in the right direction.<P>Did I miss a meeting?||||reg||1
Z||000016||fotofrank||09-30-2001||10:33 PM||||The rockers are standard. i belive I get a bit more than 104HP and don't know what the torque is. It's a good feeling when running with some 2.8 for,ulas and GTs and asked if it really is a Duke. I may not be faster but shure can keep up with an unmodified 2.8V6. Aftrer all the speed limit in most cities is 35mph and 55 to 65mph on the road. Course pacing a corvette at 85mph is a kick. <P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||6
Z||000017||Fierowrecker||09-30-2001||11:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fotofrank:<BR><B>The rockers are standard. i belive I get a bit more than 104HP and don't know what the torque is. It's a good feeling when running with some 2.8 for,ulas and GTs and asked if it really is a Duke. I may not be faster but shure can keep up with an unmodified 2.8V6. Aftrer all the speed limit in most cities is 35mph and 55 to 65mph on the road. Course pacing a corvette at 85mph is a kick. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hee Hee!<BR>I understand about the kick!<BR>On the rockers, I meant the lifters...<BR>I had roller lifters in my 86 engines, and quite a few were broken in both engines...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000018||fotofrank||10-01-2001||01:43 PM||||The lifters are stock. I only did bolt ons so far. I should also mention that the 85mph corvette pace was an "eazy" pace. I was going about 75 when he passed me and caught up very fast. And no the pedal was not to the metal!<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||10
Z||000019||erikred||10-01-2001||06:42 PM||||When is your meeting? I have alot of info you could use, but it will take me a little while to get it together. Almost any part you could want is available for this motor.<P>Erik-||||reg||14
Z||000020||erikred||10-01-2001||06:46 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Leper:<BR><B>Performace parts eh?<BR>Part numbers?<P>Super Duty block 10093306 $836.65 <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know where to get the other stuff, but where did you find the SD block?<BR>I would consider buying one for that price.<P>Erik-<P>P.S. Cloyes metal timming gears are only $70 or Mercruiser timming gears can be used for cheap.<P><p>[This message has been edited by erikred (edited 10-01-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000021||qwikgta||10-01-2001||09:25 PM||||Fierowrecker...thanks, its an 88 coupe.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/01july1_1.jpg"> <P>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000022||Leper||10-02-2001||12:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by erikred:<BR><B>  I know where to get the other stuff, but where did you find the SD block?<BR>I would consider buying one for that price.<P>Erik-<P>P.S. Cloyes metal timming gears are only $70 or Mercruiser timming gears can be used for cheap.<P>[This message has been edited by erikred (edited 10-01-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's just for a bare block. You can get all the parts I mentioned through a GM Performange Parts dealer. They have to buy the block from Kansas racing products which is the only liscensed producer of the blocks that I know of. (GM doesn't make them anymore) Kansas Racing can set you up with a complete motor that uses a cheaper chevy head too. They had a website, but It's not up anymore. Their phone number should be 785-922-6644||||reg||1
Z||000023||erikred||10-02-2001||09:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Leper:<BR><B> That's just for a bare block. You can get all the parts I mentioned through a GM Performange Parts dealer. They have to buy the block from Kansas racing products which is the only liscensed producer of the blocks that I know of. (GM doesn't make them anymore) Kansas Racing can set you up with a complete motor that uses a cheaper chevy head too. They had a website, but It's not up anymore. Their phone number should be 785-922-6644</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I thought the blocks from KRP were $2500? Is it cheaper to buy it through GM then?<P>Erik-<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000024||Leper||10-03-2001||01:41 AM||||I got the prices from https://www.spoperformanceparts.com/<P>I chose a local dealer so the prices may be different from state to state. But you can order the block from any of the dealers listed on the website. <P>According to the site, the only GMPP dealer in Ohio is is Burt Greenwald Chevrolet in Akron.<BR>Their price for the block is the same as I listed. You might want to try calling KRP and finding out their actual price for the block, just to make sure you can't get it cheaper from them.<P>The only email address I can find for them is<BR>mailto:dedonis@kans.com  but I don't know if it's still being used.||||reg||1
